+# Bug Assessment: Preserve deleted-customer orders and fix order pagination
+
+- **Slug**: ticket
+- **Created**: 2026-11-18T00:00:00+00:00
+- **Source**: pasted text
+- **Verdict**: valid
+- **Severity**: high
+
+## Report (verbatim or summarized)
+
+Support users cannot open or list orders after the customer account is deleted. The private customer-order endpoint returns 404 for a deleted customer, and order browsing returns no results after the first page. The expected behavior is to retain and expose historical order snapshots while allowing a new account to be registered with the old email and without inheriting old orders.
+
+## Symptom
+
+Deleting a customer removes the customer row but orders retain only a scalar customer id. The customer-specific private endpoint requires the customer row to exist, while paginated order responses discard totals when a requested page is empty. The order repository also computes page metadata with an off-by-one formula.
+
+## Reproduction
+
+1. Create a customer and at least one order, then delete the customer through `DELETE /api/v1/private/customer/{id}`.
+2. Request `GET /api/v1/private/orders/{orderId}` and `GET /api/v1/private/orders/customers/{customerId}`; the former/customer-specific behavior is reported as 404 and the latter explicitly returns 404 when the customer row is absent.
+3. Create more orders than the requested page size and request `GET /api/v1/private/orders?count={n}&page=1`; the reported implementation returns an empty result with zero totals instead of the second page and matching totals.
+4. Register a new customer using the deleted account email and verify it has a distinct id and no orders for that id.
+
+## Suspected Code Paths
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/order/OrderApi.java:112` — the customer-order endpoint calls `customerService.getById` and sends 404 before querying orders.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/order/facade/OrderFacadeImpl.java:936-967` — empty order pages set `recordsTotal` to zero and return before copying repository totals or `totalPages`.
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/repositories/order/OrderRepositoryImpl.java:135-253` — order filtering/pagination query and page metadata calculation; the repository returns no metadata on count zero and delegates page offset calculation.
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/utils/RepositoryHelper.java:35-45` — new-pagination offset is present, but total-pages calculation uses integer division plus one, producing incorrect totals for exact multiples.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/order/facade/OrderFacadeImpl.java:1110-1130` — order detail already treats a missing customer as a warning and leaves the order customer unset while still populating order snapshot fields.
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/customer/CustomerServiceImpl.java:100-113` — deletion removes the customer record but does not delete orders; order customer id is deliberately detached.
+
+## Root Cause Hypothesis
+
+Confidence: high. Historical order retention is already modeled by `Order.customerId`, `customerEmailAddress`, billing, and delivery fields without a customer foreign-key association. The API layer incorrectly makes the existence of the customer row a prerequisite for querying by the retained id. Separately, the facade treats an empty page as an empty dataset and loses repository count metadata, and the shared pagination helper calculates total pages incorrectly for exact page-size multiples.
+
+## Proposed Remediation
+
+**Preferred**: Remove the customer existence prerequisite from `GET /private/orders/customers/{id}`. Build an `OrderCriteria` using the requested customer id and pagination, query orders directly, and attach a readable customer only when the customer still exists; deleted-customer orders must retain their populated billing, delivery, and placed-email fields and have a null customer object. Preserve `recordsTotal` and `totalPages` even when the requested page has no rows. Correct the shared new-pagination calculation to ceiling(count / pageSize), and ensure the order response maps repository totals for all pages while retaining descending order by id.
+
+Add focused repository/facade/API regression tests covering deleted-customer lookup, customer-id filtering, empty ids, page offsets, filters, exact and out-of-range pages, and re-registration isolation. Existing physical customer deletion can remain unchanged because orders use a scalar id and a new registration receives a new customer id.
+
+**Alternatives**:
+- Add a soft-delete customer record instead of allowing detached order ids; this would preserve customer history but conflicts with the requirement that the email can be registered again and expands schema/lifecycle scope.
+
+**Files likely to change**:
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/order/OrderApi.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/order/facade/OrderFacadeImpl.java`
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/repositories/order/OrderRepositoryImpl.java`
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/utils/RepositoryHelper.java`
+- `sm-core/src/test/java/com/salesmanager/test/order/OrderTest.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/test/java/com/salesmanager/test/shop/integration/order/OrderApiIntegrationTest.java`
+
+## Tests to add or update
+
+- Customer-id order listing succeeds after customer deletion, returns retained order details with a null customer, and returns zero totals for an id with no orders.
+- Private order list returns the requested zero-based page, matching total count, ceiling total-pages, newest-first order, and stable totals for an out-of-range page with status/email/name/id filters.
+- Registering the deleted email creates a distinct customer id and does not expose the deleted customer id's orders.
+
+## Risks & Considerations
+
+- The private order endpoint must continue enforcing admin authorization; only customer existence validation should be removed.
+- Fetch joins over order collections may duplicate rows or interact with pagination; repository results and count queries should be checked against existing order fixtures.
+- Changing shared pagination metadata may affect other repositories using `RepositoryHelper`; the correction is mathematically compatible but should be regression-tested.
+- Existing data with null customer ids must remain listable through the general order endpoint and retain billing/delivery/email snapshots.
+
+## Open Questions
+
+- None; the ticket supplies the required endpoint behavior and pagination semantics.
